{"s":"antiarrhythmic-drugs","n":"Antiarrhythmic Drugs","c":"Pharmacology","y":[3,4],"a":[],"docs":5,"lead":{"t":"-​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​Antiarrhythmic​ ​drugs​ ​:​ ​Amiodarone​ ​causes​ ​ ​harmful​ ​side​ ​effects​ ​and​ ​usually​ ​given​ ​to​ ​elderly.​ ​Class​ ​IC​ ​(Flecainide,​ ​Propafenone)​ ​are​ ​safer​ ​for​ ​young​ ​patients.","u":"/blog/year-4-internal-medicine-arrhythmias","s":"Arrhythmias"},"sec":[],"src":[],"sets":[],"snip":[{"t":"-​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​Antiarrhythmic​ ​drugs​ ​:​ ​Amiodarone​ ​causes​ ​ ​harmful​ ​side​ ​effects​ ​and​ ​usually​ ​given​ ​to​ ​elderly.​ ​Class​ ​IC​ ​(Flecainide,​ ​Propafenone)​ ​are​ ​safer​ ​for​ ​young​ ​patients.","u":"/blog/year-4-internal-medicine-arrhythmias","s":"Arrhythmias"},{"t":"Restoring sinus rhythm (rhythm control): converting AF back to normal rhythm by electrical (DC) or drug cardioversion and then keeping it with antiarrhythmic drugs.","u":"/notes/papers-clinical-pharmacology-main-exam-25-january-2023","s":"Clinical Pharmacology I (MBPL 4400) main exam: 25 January 2023"},{"t":"Early afterdepolarizations (EADs) $\\rightarrow$ Prolonged repolarization (e.g., hypokalemia, antiarrhythmic drugs) $\\rightarrow$ Cell depolarizes before full repolarization $\\rightarrow$ Torsades de Pointes.","u":"/notes/arrhythmia","s":"Arrhythmias and ECG interpretation"},{"t":"-​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​Options​ ​for​ ​the​ ​long-term​ ​management​ ​of​ ​cardiac​ ​tachyarrhythmias​ ​include:​ ​antiarrhythmic​ ​drug​ ​therapy,ablation​ ​therapy​ ​or​ ​device​ ​therapy.","u":"/blog/year-4-internal-medicine-arrhythmias","s":"Arrhythmias"},{"t":"In older children, excess iodine may be present proprietary preparations used to treat asthma or in amiodarone, an antiarrhythmic drug with high iodine content.","u":"/blog/year-4-paediatrics-hypothyroidism","s":"Hypothyroidism"}],"imgs":[],"qs":[],"es":[],"rel":[{"s":"paroxysmal-supraventricular-tachycardia","n":"Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia"},{"s":"left-atrial-dilation","n":"Left Atrial Dilation"},{"s":"